ENTRY 11183 {"id":11183,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"docs/research/onecli-spike.md:8:3. **Tokens have no TTL and no IP/pod binding.** Mitigate by creating one agent per session, regenerating or deleting it on `ensure()`/delete, and using NetworkPolicy.\ndocs/decisions/0002-orphan-sweep.md:19:`session-unknown`). `active`, `failed` and `deleting` sessions are live.\ndocs/decisions/0002-orphan-sweep.md:44:  read, so a claim that changed hands between listing and deleting survives. A lone PVC goes through the same function\ndocs/decisions/0002-orphan-sweep.md:63:- A conversation whose session row is hard-deleted by hand (as the e2e cleanup does after deleting through the API) has\ndocs/decisions/0006-deletes-retry-until-done.md:9:stayed `deleting`. Nothing recovered from there: a repeated `DELETE` was deduplicated onto the failed row, the orphan\ndocs/decisions/0006-deletes-retry-until-done.md:10:sweep treats `deleting` as live (ADR 0002), and no code path resets a failed row. The sandbox, PVC and OneCLI agent\ndocs/decisions/0006-deletes-retry-until-done.md:19:- The sweep is unchanged: it still never touches `deleting` sessions. Deleting is retried by the loop that owns it, so\ndocs/decisions/0006-deletes-retry-until-done.md:28:  unaffected). A session in `deleting` accepts no new events anyway.\ndocs/decisions/0006-deletes-retry-until-done.md:32:- Rejected alternative: letting the sweep finish `deleting` sessions after a grace period. It would duplicate the delete\ndocs/decisions/0001-per-sandbox-sandboxd-token.md:47:- Recreating means deleting the claim and its workspace PVC (`workspace-<claim>`); the session's conversation state is\ndocs/session-api.md:32:| `POST /sessions/{id}/events` body `{ kind, text?, sourceEventId? }` | `202 { eventId, duplicate }` | `kind` is `message`, `steer` or `cancel`. `text` is required for `message` and `steer` (at most 64 KiB). `sourceEventId` (at most 200 characters) deduplicates. `400` invalid body, `409` session is deleting or failed, or the id belongs to another session, `410` session deleted. |\ndocs/session-api.md:34:| `GET /sessions/{id}` | `200 { sessionId, status, model: { provider, model, reasoning? }, failure?, createdAt, lastActivityAt, events: { pending, submitted, failed } }` | Answered from Postgres, so it works while the orchestrator is down. `status` is `active`, `failed`, `deleting` or `deleted`; `failure` is present only when `failed`. A session that predates per-session models reports the default model. |\ndocs/session-api.md:179:`DELETE /sessions/{id}` answers `202` and queues a `delete` row. From that moment new events get `409` (`410` once deleted). Admission is one conditional insert (`session is active`), so an event whose body was still being read when the session was deleted is refused too, and the session is marked `deleting` before the delete row is written, so every accepted event sorts before it; events\ndocs/session-api.md:203:after 5 attempts; a `delete` row has no attempt cap, because a failed delete leaves the session `deleting` with its\ndocs/session-api.md:204:sandbox, PVC and OneCLI agent alive, and the orphan sweep never touches a `deleting` session. A failing delete is\ndocs/session-api.md:216:never touched, and neither is a session that is `active`, `failed` or `deleting`, even when its sandbox can no longer work.\npackages/ingest/test/fake-db.ts:83:    if (sql.includes(\"set status = 'deleting'\")) {\npackages/ingest/test/fake-db.ts:84:      if (this.status === \"active\" || this.status === \"failed\") this.status = \"deleting\";\npackages/ingest/test/delete.test.ts:47:    expect(db.status).toBe(\"deleting\");\npackages/ingest/test/delete.test.ts:84:  it(\"answers 409 when the session started deleting in that window\", async () => {\npackages/ingest/test/delete.test.ts:88:      db.status = \"deleting\";\npackages/orchestrator/src/sweep.ts:16: * A session is an orphan's owner only if it is `deleted` or unknown. `active`, `failed` and `deleting` sessions\npackages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts:25:/** Open SSE streams by session, so deleting a session can end them. */\npackages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts:163:    // retries here and must not find \"nothing changed\" and stop. A deleting or deleted session is not ours to abort.\npackages/orchestrator/src/kube.ts:118: * first: its Sandbox owns the Pod, and a PVC that a Pod still mounts only finishes deleting after the Pod.\npackages/orchestrator/src/kube.ts:147:        `SandboxClaim ${claimName} is not labelled for this session: not deleting it`,\npackages/orchestrator/src/kube.ts:164:        `timed out deleting ${claimName}: claim ${claimPresent ? \"present\" : \"gone\"}, pvc ${pvcPresent ? \"present\" : \"gone\"}`,\npackages/session-core/src/store.ts:268:    \"update inbox.sessions set status = 'deleting', last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1 and status in ('active', 'failed')\",\npackages/ingest/test/fake-db.ts:83:    if (sql.includes(\"set status = 'deleting'\")) {\n    45\t      else res.destroy();\n    46\t    });\n    47\t  });\n    48\t}\n    49\t\n    50\tasync function handle(req: IncomingMessage, res: ServerResponse, deps: IngestDeps): Promise<void> {\n    51\t  const url = new URL(req.url ?? \"/\", \"http://localhost\");\n    52\t  const parts = url.pathname.split(\"/\").filter(Boolean);\n    53\t  const method = req.method ?? \"GET\";\n    54\t\n    55\t  if (method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/healthz\") {\n    56\t    sendJson(res, 200, { status: \"ok\" });\n    57\t    return;\n    58\t  }\n    59\t  if (method === \"GET\" && url.pathname === \"/readyz\") {\n    60\t    // Ready means \"can accept events\": the schema is migrated and the database answers. The orchestrator is\n    61\t    // deliberately not checked.\n    62\t    if (!deps.schemaReady()) {\n    63\t      sendJson(res, 503, { status: \"migrating\" });\n    64\t      return;\n    65\t    }\n    66\t    try {\n    67\t      await deps.pool.query(\"select 1\");\n    68\t      sendJson(res, 200, { status: \"ready\" });\n    69\t    } catch {\n    70\t      sendJson(res, 503, { status: \"database unavailable\" });\n    71\t    }\n    72\t    return;\n    73\t  }\n    74\t\n    75\t  if (!deps.schemaReady()) {\n    76\t    sendJson(res, 503, { error: \"starting\" }, { \"retry-after\": \"2\" });\n    77\t    return;\n    78\t  }\n    79\t\n    80\t  // Every route below is behind this one check.\n    81\t  const principal = await deps.authenticate(req.headers);\n    82\t  if (principal === undefined) {\n    83\t    sendJson(res, 401, { error: \"unauthorized\" }, { \"www-authenticate\": \"Bearer\" });\n    84\t    return;\n    85\t  }\n    86\t\n    87\t  if (method === \"POST\" && url.pathname === \"/sessions\") {\n    88\t    await postSession(req, res, deps, principal);\n    89\t    return;\n    90\t  }\n    91\t  if (parts[0] !== \"sessions\" || parts[1] === undefined) {\n    92\t    sendJson(res, 404, { error: \"not found\" });\n    93\t    return;\n    94\t  }\n    95\t  const session = await ownedSession(deps.pool, parts[1], principal);\n    96\t  if (session === undefined) {\n    97\t    // Unknown id and someone else's id look the same: the API does not reveal that a session exists.\n    98\t    sendJson(res, 404, { error: \"session not found\" });\n    99\t    return;\n   100\t  }\n   101\t\n   102\t  if (parts.length === 2 && method === \"GET\") {\n   103\t    const summary = await summarize(deps.pool, session);\n   104\t    sendJson(res, 200, {\n   105\t      sessionId: session.id,\n   106\t      status: summary.status,\n   107\t      model: modelOf(session, deps.models),\n   108\t      ...(session.repo === null ? {} : { repo: session.repo }),\n   109\t      ...(session.failure === null ? {} : { failure: session.failure }),\n   110\t      createdAt: session.createdAt.toISOString(),\n   111\t      lastActivityAt: summary.lastActivityAt.toISOString(),\n   112\t      events: summary.events,\n   113\t    });\n   114\t    return;\n   115\t  }\n   116\t  if (parts.length === 2 && method === \"DELETE\") {\n   117\t    await queueDelete(deps.pool, session, res);\n   118\t    return;\n   119\t  }\n   120\t  if (parts.length === 3 && parts[2] === \"events\" && method === \"POST\") {\n   121\t    await postEvent(req, res, deps.pool, session, principal);\n   122\t    return;\n   123\t  }\n   124\t  if (parts.length === 3 && parts[2] === \"stream\" && method === \"GET\") {\n   125\t    if (session.status === \"deleted\") {\n   126\t      sendJson(res, 410, { error: \"session deleted\" });\n   127\t      return;\n   128\t    }\n   129\t    proxyStream(req, res, deps.orchestratorUrl, session.id);\n   130\t    return;\n   131\t  }\n   132\t  sendJson(res, 404, { error: \"not found\" });\n   133\t}\n   134\t\n   135\t/** Sessions that predate migration 002 have no stored model: they run the default. */\n   136\tfunction modelOf(session: SessionRow, policy: ModelPolicy): ModelChoice {\n   137\t  return session.model ?? policy.default;\n   138\t}\n   139\t\n   140\tasync function postSession(\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 11219 {"id":11219,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"## Findings\n\n### 1. Interrupted DELETE can leave a session permanently stuck deleting\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/ingest/src/server.ts:248\n- What happens: If ingest crashes or the database becomes unavailable after the status update commits but before the delete event is inserted, the session remains `deleting` without an event for the orchestrator to process. It rejects new events, while its sandbox and other resources remain allocated. Recovery requires the client to retry DELETE.\n- Evidence: `await requestDelete(pool, session.id);` is followed by a separate `await enqueueEvent(pool, ...)`.\n- Fix idea: Commit the status transition and delete-event insertion in one database transaction, preserving the ordering guarantees for accepted events.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
DONE
